---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Devices"
  description="Published device integration notes for auroraADE."
  current="devices"
>
  <header class="page-heading">
    <p class="page-context">December Reach / Documentation</p>
    <h1>Devices</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">Published device integration notes for auroraADE.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="document-section" id="status">
    <header class="document-heading">
      <h2>Integration status</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="document-body">
      <p class="document-intro">These entries preserve the last published project status. They are not live build or device checks.</p>
      <dl class="status-list">
        <div class="status-row">
          <dt>
            <span class="status-name">Desktop</span>
            <span class="status-value">Pending</span>
          </dt>
          <dd>Runtime integration pending. The browser runtime was not connected to a desktop build in the last published status.</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="status-row">
          <dt>
            <span class="status-name">Mobile</span>
            <span class="status-value">Unavailable</span>
          </dt>
          <dd>No mobile build was available in the last published status.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="document-section" id="target">
    <header class="document-heading">
      <h2>Platform target</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="document-body">
      <p>auroraADE's documented target architecture is x86_64. The wider Fabric Dessert CPU integration boundary is designed to accommodate ARM 32-bit, ARM 64-bit, x86 32-bit and x86 64-bit integrations; that broader boundary should not be confused with auroraADE's own target.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/architecture/">Architecture documentation</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
